This is an excellent architectural design. Your notification schema natively supports the **"Exclude Creator" pattern**. By passing BOTH the TARGET_ROLE and the USER_ID, the system intelligently notifies all the Checkers in the department *except* the person who created the request, preventing them from receiving an alert to approve their own batch.
To implement this perfectly, we need to extract the ALLOWED_ROLE_ID from the WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS table whenever a batch advances, and route the notification accordingly.
Here is the complete, professional implementation for all lifecycle events (Creation, Intermediate Approval, Final Approval, and Rejection).
### 1. Update your NotificationWriterService.java
First, ensure your Notification Writer Service has a streamlined method to handle this outbox insert.
```java
import org.springframework.jdbc.core.JdbcTemplate;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Propagation;
import org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional;
import java.util.UUID;

@Service
public class NotificationWriterService {

    private final JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate;

    public NotificationWriterService(JdbcTemplate jdbcTemplate) {
        this.jdbcTemplate = jdbcTemplate;
    }

    /**
     * Inserts a notification into the Outbox table.
     * If TARGET_ROLE is provided and USER_ID is provided, USER_ID is explicitly EXCLUDED.
     * If TARGET_ROLE is null, it sends strictly to the USER_ID.
     */
    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void createNotification(String userId, String targetRole, String message, String linkUrl, String aggregateId, String source) {
        String sql = """
            INSERT INTO NOTIFICATIONS 
            (EVENT_ID, USER_ID, TARGET_ROLE, MESSAGE, LINK_URL, AGGREGATE_ID, EVENT_SOURCE, EVENT_TIMESTAMP) 
            VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)
        """;
        
        // Generate RAW GUID for Oracle
        String eventId = UUID.randomUUID().toString().replace("-", "").toUpperCase();
        
        jdbcTemplate.update(sql, eventId, userId, targetRole, message, linkUrl, aggregateId, source);
    }
}

```
